All calculations executed. Summary of what the tool runs established before the final JSON:

- OLS on 5,921 train pairs: β₀ = −0.063688, β₁ = −0.015439, s² = 21.7632 bps², t = 1.960365, R² ≈ 0.00024; within-segment residual lag-1 corr = 0.000292 (5,910 adjacent pairs).
- Validation (n = 1,775): MSE 2.80993 vs zero-baseline 2.80385 (model slightly worse); prediction-interval half-width ≈ 9.15 bps covers 1,774/1,775 = 99.94% of y (over-coverage from train variance being ~2.8× validation variance); the narrow mean interval (0.12–0.26 bps) contains only 248/1,775 y's, as expected for an interval meant for the mean, not y.
- Robust rule with k = 10 bps, λ = .04, v = s²: m̂ ∈ [−0.179, 0.080] bps and u ∈ [0.119, 0.264] bps, so max robust edge is −10.03 bps (short side) → 0 trades, mean net 0.000 bps/opportunity (still 0 trades even at k = 0, since |m̂| < u everywhere).
- Closed-form position matched direct grid maximization on 64 cases (50 random + 14 edge/tie cases) with max objective difference = 0; tie cases returned exactly 0.0.

